---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import clinic from '../data/clinic.json';

const effective = '13 October 2026';
const address = `${clinic.address.line1}, ${clinic.address.line2}, ${clinic.address.city}, ${clinic.address.state} ${clinic.address.postalCode}`;
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${clinic.shortName}`}
  description={`How ${clinic.name} handles information on drtalalhomeo.in and in the TalalClinic tool it uses to manage its Google Business Profile.`}
>
  <article class="article">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span>/</span> Privacy policy
      </div>

      <header class="article-head">
        <div class="article-meta">
          <span>Effective {effective}</span>
        </div>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          What this website and our TalalClinic tool do with information — in short, very
          little. This page covers the website drtalalhomeo.in and the TalalClinic tool only.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="article-body">
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          This website is run by {clinic.name}, a homoeopathy clinic at {address}. "We" and
          "the clinic" on this page mean that clinic.
        </p>

        <h2>What the website does not collect</h2>
        <p>
          The website is a set of plain pages. It has no sign-up, no login, no contact form and
          no online booking, so there is nowhere on it to enter personal details. We do not use
          analytics or advertising trackers, and the site sets no cookies of its own.
        </p>

        <h2>What is recorded automatically</h2>
        <p>
          Like almost every web server, ours keeps a technical log of requests: the IP address,
          the date and time, the page requested and the browser type. We use this only to keep
          the site running and to spot abuse. Log files are deleted automatically after about
          14 days. We do not use them to identify individual visitors.
        </p>

        <h2>Services from other companies</h2>
        <p>Some parts of the site are provided by other companies, who receive your IP address when your browser loads them:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Fonts</strong> supplies the typefaces on every page.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Maps</strong> supplies the map on the home page and the Visit page,
            and may set its own cookies.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The site also links to WhatsApp, Google Maps, Google reviews, Instagram and Facebook.
          Once you follow one of those links you are on that company's service, under its own
          privacy policy.
        </p>

        <h2>When you call or message us</h2>
        <p>
          If you phone the clinic or message us on WhatsApp, we receive your number and whatever
          you choose to tell us. We use it to reply and to arrange your visit. WhatsApp is
          operated by Meta, which handles messages under its own privacy policy.
        </p>

        <h2>Patient records</h2>
        <p>
          Anything you share in a consultation is part of your medical care and is not handled
          through this website. This page does not describe it. Please ask at the clinic if you
          have questions about your consultation records.
        </p>

        <h2>Reviews shown on the site</h2>
        <p>
          The site shows short excerpts of reviews that patients posted publicly on Google, with
          the reviewer's name shortened. If one of them is yours and you would like it removed,
          tell us and we will take it down.
        </p>

        <h2>The TalalClinic tool and Google data</h2>
        <p>
          TalalClinic is an internal tool that the clinic uses to publish its own updates. It
          is not a public app: it has no sign-up and no users other than the clinic.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>What it accesses.</strong> It connects to Google's Business Profile API with
            the <code style="overflow-wrap: anywhere;">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/business.manage</code> permission, granted
            by the Google account that manages the clinic's own Business Profile.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>What it does with that access.</strong> It creates posts on the clinic's own
            Business Profile listing, and can remove posts it created. It does not read or
            reply to reviews, and it does not access any other business's profile or any other
            person's Google data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>What it stores.</strong> Only the access credential that Google issues to
            the clinic, kept on a private server that the clinic controls. It stores no personal
            information about patients or website visitors.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Sharing.</strong> Nothing obtained through Google's API is sold, shared with
            anyone else, or used for advertising.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          TalalClinic's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
          <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
          including the Limited Use requirements. The clinic can withdraw the tool's access at
          any time from its Google account settings.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions and requests</h2>
        <p>
          If you have contacted us and would like your number or messages deleted, or you have
          any question about this page, call
          <a href={`tel:${clinic.phone.tel}`}>{clinic.phone.display}</a>, message us on
          <a href={clinic.links.whatsapp} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp</a>,
          or write to {clinic.name}, {address}.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
        <p>
          If what we do changes, we will update this page and the effective date at the top.
          See also our <a href="/terms">terms and conditions</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
